1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,957
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,687
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,577
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, and so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,637
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,857
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:10,980
Believe in wonder.

17
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:21,137
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:24,177
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We'll live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,617
We don't want to live ordinary lives.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,757
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:42,760
We live in wonderland.

26
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:56,917
Nami, how you feeling?

27
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,235
Are you completely recovered
from your illness already?

28
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:02,480
Sure am. I feel great.

29
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:04,130
Hey!

30
00:02:04,213 --> 00:02:05,917
How about we go say
goodbye to the old doctor

31
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,797
lady and that Dalton guy from the village?

32
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:08,937
Don't be so thoughtless.

33
00:02:09,020 --> 00:02:10,597
We need to leave Chopper alone with Dr.

34
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:11,510
E for a while.

35
00:02:11,593 --> 00:02:13,337
He lived with her for six years.

36
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:15,257
We should let them say goodbye in peace.

37
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:17,557
I'm sure it's going to be
really sad for them both.

38
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:18,470
Dr.

39
00:02:18,553 --> 00:02:22,717
E acts all tough in front of us, but deep
down, I think she really is a kind person.

40
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:25,797
So, we're just going to leave
without saying anything to her?

41
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:26,998
Yeah, that's right.

42
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:28,317
Once Chopper comes back,

43
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:31,988
we'll go straight down the
mountain and set sail to Alabasta.

44
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:34,042
Sounds good to you, right, Vivi?

45
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:37,640
Yes, now that we have a
doctor coming with us. Doctor?

46
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,317
Well, in that case, I'll go
ahead and get the ropeway ready.

47
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,240
Hey, Luffy! Give me a hand!

48
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:45,714
I didn't even know there was a ropeway!

49
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:46,960
So cool!

50
00:02:58,100 --> 00:02:59,420
Well, look at that.

51
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:02,719
It seems as if we have a
couple of patients missing.

52
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:04,457
Yes, they all left.

53
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:06,422
Directly disobeying your orders.

54
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:08,460
Oh, I see.

55
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,740
What am I going to do with them?

56
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:21,000
Dr. Ayn!

57
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:24,300
Dr. Ayn!

58
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:28,140
I need to talk to you right now.

59
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:30,877
Chopper, where have you been all day?

60
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:32,477
Hurry up and get downstairs.

61
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:34,917
You can help the men
take the cannons outside.

62
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,437
Please listen, Doctorine.

63
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:38,097
I'm going to become a pirate.

64
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:40,117
I'm leaving with the others right now.

65
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,340
What did you say?

66
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:42,795
I'm going out to sea.

67
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:45,497
I'm coming on board with
them as the ship's doctor.

68
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:47,317
I'm going to travel everywhere.

69
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:49,224
Stop this foolishness, Chopper.

70
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:53,260
Now listen, you know
you're my only assistant.

71
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:56,717
I'm the one who taught you
everything you know about medicine.

72
00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:00,900
Do you really feel no gratitude
at all for what I've done? No.

73
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:02,276
No, that isn't true.

74
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:04,917
I'm incredibly grateful to you, Doctorine.

75
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,860
And I'll always love this land.

76
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:09,589
It's where I met you
and Doctor, after all.

77
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:10,550
Hmm.

78
00:04:10,633 --> 00:04:11,617
Then you can just stay here.

79
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:13,817
If you think you can
find another home as nice

80
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:15,817
as this one somewhere
in the outside world,

81
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:17,194
you're sadly mistaken.

82
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:19,557
Those pirates aren't good
for anything, Chopper.

83
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:22,497
You'll end up dead on some
vagabond sword in no time.

84
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:23,780
I can accept that.

85
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:27,022
Don't sound so sure of yourself.

86
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:30,737
A reindeer going out to sea, that's the
most ridiculous thing I've ever heard of.

87
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:34,200
Yeah, I am a reindeer,
but still, I'm a man.

88
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:40,300
You can talk tough for now, but
you're still my assistant, Chopper.

89
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:43,237
If you want to leave, you're going
to have to go through me first.

90
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,379
Do you understand?

91
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:46,370
Dr. Reed.

92
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:54,177
You're still afraid of your own shadow,
and you're telling me you're a man?

93
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:56,300
Oh, please, don't make me laugh.

94
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:57,810
But, Dr.

95
00:04:57,893 --> 00:05:00,000
Eam, these pirates, don't you see?

96
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:01,240
Shut up!

97
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:02,500
Let's go!

98
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:05,920
They like me.

99
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:07,320
Quiet, you!

100
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,520
No, I'm not gonna let you leave me!

101
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:17,640
You're staying!

102
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:21,980
Get back here, Chopper!

103
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:26,020
You can't escape!

104
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:30,715
I wonder what all that noise is about.

105
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:32,170
Who knows?

106
00:05:32,253 --> 00:05:35,017
Whatever's going on, we'd better
hurry and get all this stuff outside.

107
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:36,337
If we aren't careful, Dr.

108
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:39,137
Karoo will start using
us for target practice.

109
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:41,340
Don't exaggerate. Come back!

110
00:05:42,620 --> 00:05:45,160
I won't let you get away from me, Chopper!

111
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:47,835
They're scared of us!

112
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,261
What's going on?

113
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:53,397
There's a lot of noise
coming from the castle.

114
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:57,637
How inconsiderate, making all that noise
when those two are trying to say goodbye.

115
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:59,308
That's just downright rude.

116
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:02,700
I'm sorry, Dr.

117
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:06,644
Eaton, but I want to go out and
see the world beyond this island.

118
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:14,437
Why could someone like you
do on a pirate ship, Chopper?

119
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:18,226
Are you going to try to live some
fantasy like that, old quack?

120
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:20,960
No, you're wrong.

121
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,580
It wasn't a fantasy.

122
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:28,180
Doctor's research was finally completed
before he died. Oh, finally. Here he comes.

123
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,560
What's going on?

124
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:33,280
He's being chased.

125
00:06:34,340 --> 00:06:36,960
Hey, we got the ropeway ready to go.

126
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:40,297
Everyone, get on the sleigh.

127
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:41,757
We're going to head down the mountain.

128
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:42,670
Hurry!

129
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:55,700
Hey, look at that!

130
00:06:55,900 --> 00:06:57,547
What the hell is that thing?

131
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:01,349
That's the witch's sleigh!

132
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:37,800
What was that thing?

133
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:39,120
It looked like Dr.

134
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:40,277
Correa's reindeer.

135
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:42,397
And those pirates were
riding in the sleigh.

136
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:43,877
What's going on up there anyway?

137
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,372
What happened to Wapol?

138
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:47,112
I hope Dalton's alright.

139
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,120
That was fun!

140
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:55,337
Hey, reindeer, can we do that again?

141
00:07:55,420 --> 00:07:57,657
You idiot, we don't have time for that!

142
00:07:57,740 --> 00:07:59,269
I thought I was gonna die!

143
00:07:59,380 --> 00:08:00,321
Hey, where am I?

144
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:01,361
What's going on?

145
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:04,200
Oh, Sanji, you're awake! You okay?

146
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:12,336
You really think that was
the best way to say goodbye?

147
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:19,380
A pet I was taking care of is being looked
after by someone else now. That's all.

148
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:25,220
Besides, I don't like long goodbyes.

149
00:08:31,780 --> 00:08:32,610
Come on!

150
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:34,240
We have work to do!

151
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:37,560
We have to prepare a fitting
send-off! That hurts.

152
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:42,680
I've finally done it! This is it!

153
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:43,820
This reaction!

154
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:46,078
I've been waiting 30 years for this.

155
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:49,760
Doctor, it wasn't a fantasy
like she said, right?

156
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,237
You finished your work.

157
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:52,967
You accomplished your dream.

158
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:55,800
Or was that all a lie, too?

159
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:58,160
I've done it, Chopper!

160
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:00,180
My research is a success!

161
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:04,157
Did you lie because you knew how sad I'd
be if you died without completing it?

162
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:07,457
Nothing is impossible for a
man who raises a pirate flag.

163
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:09,340
Please say it again, Doctor!

164
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:16,757
All right young man, are you ready?

165
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:22,160
Yes, listen to me Kureha this dust special

166
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:30,800
What are you doing just shut up and watch?

167
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:40,617
It's coming from the castle Is Waffle
setting off fireworks or something?

168
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:43,417
No, those are cannon blasts
What's happening up there?

169
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:44,737
Watch for cannonballs.

170
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:47,597
It's too dark to see what
they're doing up there?

171
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:48,510
Dr.

172
00:09:48,593 --> 00:09:51,831
Corgi, all the cannons have
been fired Then light them up.

173
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:54,430
Look

174
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:04,200
Oh, cool.

175
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:05,890
Yeah.

176
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:08,030
Wow.

177
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:14,360
After 30 years, this dust
finally completes my research.

178
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:17,620
This is just absolutely amazing.

179
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:22,456
I still can't understand
what that idiot was thinking.

180
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:25,660
I will make cherry blossoms
bloom in this country.

181
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:29,984
Once my invention is perfected,
this country is as good as saved.

182
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,677
Get out of here, you crazy quack!

183
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:34,936
I thought lizard eyeballs would work!

184
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:40,200
This is no ordinary red dust, Pereja.

185
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:42,837
This dust is designed
to attach itself to the

186
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:45,517
white snowflakes as they
come down from the sky.

187
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:50,188
The white snow will then become a beautiful
shade of pink for everyone to see.

188
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:57,970
Doctor!

189
00:10:58,680 --> 00:10:59,510
Doctor!

190
00:10:59,593 --> 00:11:00,820
Doctor Eve!

191
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,497
I promise you, I'm not going to shoot you.

192
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:38,410
See?

193
00:11:38,493 --> 00:11:41,120
My name is Hiriluk. Dr. Hiriluk.

194
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:43,940
Tony, Tony Chopper.

195
00:11:44,080 --> 00:11:44,962
Cool name, huh?

196
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:47,831
Anyway, that's what I'm going to call you.

197
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,235
You're going to become a great doctor.

198
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:51,820
I'll make sure of it.

199
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:01,727
Even if I should disappear right
now, my dream will come true.

200
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:04,640
I've had a marvelous life.

201
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:10,720
Thank you so much, Chopper.

202
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:25,940
Now have a safe trip, my stupid son.

203
00:12:57,700 --> 00:12:59,897
Moonlit night, cherry
blossoms are in the air.

204
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:01,215
How can we not party?

205
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:03,879
They're a handful.

206
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:08,394
I hate to tell you, but your new
friends are about as crazy as they come.

207
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:11,760
My friends? That's right.

208
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:13,777
These guys can really be a lot to handle,

209
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:16,837
but now that you're one of us, you're
going to have to get used to it.

210
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:17,750
Yes!

211
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:18,910
Come on!

212
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:23,159
Conney, what in the world were you
doing frozen in the river like that?

213
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:27,597
That bird, ten berries, says he
slipped and fell into the river.

214
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:28,677
He's a clumsy one.

215
00:13:28,760 --> 00:13:30,100
Be quiet, Mr. Bushido.

216
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:32,360
Huh? Yeah?

217
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:35,857
He said that the guy named Zoro was
swimming in the river and disappeared.

218
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,117
He thought Zoro was in trouble,

219
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:39,997
so he jumped into the river to help
and ended up getting frozen in it.

220
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,609
So this is all your fault!

221
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:45,857
So you were really able to understand
everything Kari was saying?

222
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:46,770
Yes.

223
00:13:46,853 --> 00:13:50,437
I'm still technically half-animal by
nature, so I can understand what they say.

224
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:51,960
You can talk to animals?

225
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:53,300
Oh, wow, Chopper.

226
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:57,757
Between your medical skills and talking to
animals, you've got some amazing talents.

227
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:58,740
Don't be silly!

228
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:02,377
You jerk-flattering me like that isn't
going to make me happy or anything!

229
00:14:02,460 --> 00:14:03,636
He sure looks happy.

230
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:06,937
Hey, what did you mean about
Chopper's medical skills anyway?

231
00:14:07,020 --> 00:14:10,417
Well, Chopper here is a doctor
and a first-rate one at that.

232
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:11,330
Dr.

233
00:14:11,413 --> 00:14:14,528
Kureha taught him everything
there is to know about medicine.

234
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:15,550
Impossible.

235
00:14:15,633 --> 00:14:17,557
Chopper, are you seriously a doctor?

236
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:19,660
How cool! No way!

237
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:21,717
Really, Luffy, if you didn't know that,

238
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:24,197
what did you think Chopper was
when you asked him to join us?

239
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:26,809
The talking, transforming
reindeer monster.

240
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:27,950
Backup food.

241
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:30,850
Wait, oh no!

242
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:33,937
I was in such a big hurry, I
left my medical bag behind.

243
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:35,237
It had all of my tools in it.

244
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:36,150
Your bag?

245
00:14:36,233 --> 00:14:37,099
But isn't this it?

246
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:38,750
Huh?

247
00:14:38,833 --> 00:14:39,663
That is my bag.

248
00:14:39,746 --> 00:14:41,481
It was in the back of the sleigh.

249
00:14:42,140 --> 00:14:42,970
What was that?

250
00:14:43,620 --> 00:14:44,620
What do you mean?

251
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:48,955
Weren't you the one who packed the
sleigh and got it ready for the trip?

252
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:21,020
That's amazing.

253
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:24,277
Doctorine must have known
what you were planning to do

254
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:27,654
even before you had decided
to leave the island with us.

255
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:30,760
What a kind woman.

256
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,118
Hello, I got snot on the chopsticks!

257
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:35,160
Here, eat it!

258
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,200
Stop, eat it!

259
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:43,657
Those guys, can't they see you're
having a sentimental moment here?

260
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:44,858
I'm sorry, Chopper.

261
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:46,410
Chopper?

262
00:15:46,740 --> 00:15:47,600
You too?

263
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:52,540
All right, Straw Hat crew, attention!

264
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:54,880
Listen, all of you!

265
00:15:55,540 --> 00:16:02,060
Come on, Sanji!

266
00:16:02,780 --> 00:16:03,610
Oh, no.

267
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:06,600
Hey, come on, you guys!

268
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:10,100
Oh, we're crazy.

269
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:23,420
I propose a toast to
our new friend, Chopper!

270
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:36,057
I wonder if they've made
it off the island yet.

271
00:16:36,140 --> 00:16:36,970
You know,

272
00:16:37,053 --> 00:16:40,677
that reindeer friend of yours is a
first-rate doctor with a first-rate heart.

273
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:42,437
I'm very glad to have known him.

274
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:46,991
Those cherry blossoms of hero looks
really did lead to something miraculous.

275
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:50,257
But who'd have thought the
miracle would be that clumsy

276
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:53,281
reindeer going out to sea
with a group of pirates?

277
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:54,440
That kid.

278
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:57,527
Acting like he's a grown
man all of a sudden.

279
00:16:58,040 --> 00:17:00,864
I have a feeling I'll
make a fine ship's doctor.

280
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:05,695
So what are your plans now that Wapol
has gone from the island for good?

281
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:07,457
For a long time,

282
00:17:07,540 --> 00:17:11,599
I worked as the captain of the guard
under Walpole's tyrannical rule.

283
00:17:12,380 --> 00:17:15,437
That's something that I still
need to make amends for.

284
00:17:15,520 --> 00:17:17,991
I was thinking about leaving this country.

285
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,917
Trusting the citizens
to make a better land

286
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,647
for themselves without
me here as a reminder.

287
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:24,370
I see.

288
00:17:24,453 --> 00:17:26,220
Is that what you've decided to do?

289
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:28,430
No.

290
00:17:28,513 --> 00:17:32,296
I realize that leaving here isn't
the way to make up for past mistakes.

291
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:34,968
This country is rid of
its corrupt monarchy.

292
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:38,977
Its citizens are preparing to build
a new country that's all their own.

293
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:40,597
And I think if I stayed here,

294
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:45,057
I could find a way to help them build it
into the country that it's meant to be.

295
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:46,297
Maybe that will help,

296
00:17:46,380 --> 00:17:50,717
by washing away some of the guilt that
I've carried around with me for so long.

297
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:51,630
Well,

298
00:17:51,713 --> 00:17:54,377
it seems to me that you
certainly do possess the

299
00:17:54,460 --> 00:17:57,225
strength of heart to take
care of this country.

300
00:17:57,880 --> 00:18:00,939
Strength of heart is needed
to look after a country.

301
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,097
And it can be difficult to come by,

302
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:06,997
but I once saw it from a girl who was
no more than ten years old at the time.

303
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:09,020
Ah, the world's summit again.

304
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:10,997
What a useless event this is.

305
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:12,997
I'm tired of coming to
this thing every year.

306
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:14,374
Absolutely right, sir.

307
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:19,908
I wonder how much longer Drum
Kingdom can continue like this.

308
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:23,808
The rift between the monarchy
and the citizens keeps growing.

309
00:18:25,140 --> 00:18:26,100
Oh, look!

310
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,769
It's the King of Alabasta!

311
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:29,560
Cobra Nefertari.

312
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:37,215
A king who is known throughout the
world for his benevolence and wisdom.

313
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:39,811
The revolutionist dragon.

314
00:18:39,980 --> 00:18:42,215
This man's beliefs are very dangerous.

315
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:46,917
As world leaders, we should be aware of
the threat he poses to our countries.

316
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
In as little as five or six years,

317
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:52,924
he will likely become a prominent
enemy opposed to our interests.

318
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:56,517
Well, I don't know about the
rest of your dumb countries,

319
00:18:56,600 --> 00:19:01,397
But mine's governed too well for my citizens
to be led astray by some revolutionist.

320
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:04,157
Go ahead and capture them if
you want, but leave me out.

321
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:05,181
It's ridiculous.

322
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:06,510
Fool!

323
00:19:06,593 --> 00:19:07,820
You are a selfish fool!

324
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:11,077
Why do you think we've all
gathered here at the World Summit?

325
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:13,360
Just act responsibly for once.

326
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:15,960
No one talks to me like that!

327
00:19:17,640 --> 00:19:20,877
Well, that summit was as
unenjoyable as all the rest of them.

328
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:22,320
Huh? That girl.

329
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:25,440
She's that idiot Cobra's daughter.

330
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:30,470
Oh, no!

331
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:31,837
My hand must have slipped!

332
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:32,750
What are you doing?

333
00:19:32,833 --> 00:19:33,663
Sorry!

334
00:19:33,746 --> 00:19:34,597
Princess Vivian!

335
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:35,510
Oh, excuse me.

336
00:19:35,593 --> 00:19:38,617
If I'm not mistaken, you're the
princess of Alabasta Kingdom.

337
00:19:38,700 --> 00:19:39,530
Wow!

338
00:19:39,613 --> 00:19:41,477
It must suck to have
such a pathetic father.

339
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:42,390
Dammit!

340
00:19:42,473 --> 00:19:43,303
What do you think you're doing?

341
00:19:43,386 --> 00:19:45,240
No, stop, Yigarum. I'm fine.

342
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:47,960
My apologies.

343
00:19:48,280 --> 00:19:50,456
I didn't look where I was going, sir.

344
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:53,137
That is quite a child.

345
00:19:53,220 --> 00:19:57,037
At a world summit like this where all of
the most powerful leaders are gathered,

346
00:19:57,120 --> 00:19:58,237
tensions tend to run high.

347
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:00,497
The slightest argument
can trigger an Alto war.

348
00:20:00,580 --> 00:20:03,051
Knowing that, she refused to make a scene.

349
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:06,320
She's so young to be so wise.

350
00:20:06,820 --> 00:20:08,600
What an annoying little brat!

351
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:09,860
Let's go, Dalton!

352
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:11,900
Forgive us.

353
00:20:18,660 --> 00:20:21,440
You made me so proud today, Princess V.

354
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:28,477
That princess had great strength of
heart indeed and that hasn't changed.

355
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:34,460
She's remained strong all these
years she would make anyone.

356
00:20:38,580 --> 00:20:43,277
Dalton please the desire to care for
our country hasn't faded from within us!

357
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:46,257
Either allow us to do
something we want to help?

358
00:20:46,340 --> 00:20:47,516
Build a new country.

359
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:55,080
Here you look.

360
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:58,897
This country will be reborn
as you always wished it to be.

361
00:20:58,980 --> 00:21:02,180
Just like your son, Chopper. Dalton!

362
00:21:02,320 --> 00:21:03,614
You need to hear this!

363
00:21:05,320 --> 00:21:08,397
I just remembered something
important that I forgot to tell you!

364
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:09,310
What is it?

365
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:10,376
Take a look at this!

366
00:21:12,220 --> 00:21:13,050
It's him!

367
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:15,917
That's the Straw Hat
Pirate who defeated Wapol.

368
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,000
We're sure of it.

369
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:20,117
You mean he has a 30 million
berry bounty on his head?

370
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:21,740
Are you certain? Goodness.

371
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:24,748
They're quite a band
of rogues, aren't they?

372
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:26,714
Where'd you find this?

373
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:29,977
Well, uh, I completely forgot
to report this to you, Dalton.

374
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:30,942
I'm very sorry.

375
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:33,572
I guess it all happened about a week ago.

376
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:38,369
A man who seemed to be a random traveler
showed up one day over in Robeltown.

377
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:42,417
Strangely, it was a day
without any snowfall.

378
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:44,877
We have no idea where
on the island he landed.

379
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:47,060
Anyway, he told us something.

380
00:21:47,380 --> 00:21:49,437
The man said he was
hunting down Blackbeard,

381
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:52,137
the pirate, who recently
attacked our island with his men.

382
00:21:52,220 --> 00:21:56,077
And then, once he realized that
Blackbeard had already left, he said...

383
00:21:56,160 --> 00:21:58,237
In that case, I have one more question.

384
00:21:58,320 --> 00:22:01,897
Has a pirate wearing a Straw Hat
come through this area recently?

385
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:05,957
We didn't know, so he showed us
the wanted poster and said...

386
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:08,940
Well, if the guy I
described does show up...

387
00:22:10,060 --> 00:22:11,080
If he does?

388
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:12,915
Deliver this message.

389
00:22:13,120 --> 00:22:16,473
I will wait for him in Alabasta
for ten days and no more.

390
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:17,840
Don't forget.

391
00:22:19,900 --> 00:22:20,730
Hey!

392
00:22:20,940 --> 00:22:22,180
Hold on a sec!

393
00:22:22,460 --> 00:22:24,017
You didn't tell us your name!

394
00:22:24,100 --> 00:22:24,930
Oh, yes.

395
00:22:25,013 --> 00:22:26,500
I forgot about that.

396
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:29,900
The name's Ace, gentlemen.

397
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:33,711
If you tell the Straw Hat
Pirate, then he'll know who I am.

398
00:22:39,280 --> 00:22:40,620
Hey, catch that guy!

399
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:42,857
He ate and didn't pay his
cab in the restaurant!

400
00:22:42,940 --> 00:22:44,177
Just give him the message!

401
00:22:44,260 --> 00:22:45,090
Thanks!

402
00:22:48,420 --> 00:22:51,067
So he'll be waiting in
Alabasta for ten days.

403
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:56,577
Excuse me, Doctor, but
is there something wrong?

404
00:22:56,660 --> 00:22:57,660
You look puzzled.

405
00:22:57,880 --> 00:22:59,177
Tell me something, Dalton.

406
00:22:59,260 --> 00:23:01,907
Have you ever heard of
the man Goldie, Roger?

407
00:23:02,160 --> 00:23:02,990
Goldie?

408
00:23:03,073 --> 00:23:04,600
Do you mean Gold Roger?

409
00:23:04,960 --> 00:23:05,940
I guess.

410
00:23:06,260 --> 00:23:07,907
Is that what he goes by now?

411
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:11,040
From the looks of this,

412
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:17,220
the guy Chopper left this island and headed
out to Sea Whiff is no ordinary pirate.

413
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:19,360
The spirit of D.

414
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:21,980
It still lives.

415
00:23:22,340 --> 00:23:23,420
What do you know?

416
00:23:30,780 --> 00:23:32,680
So what is Alabasta, then?

417
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:34,937
It's the country where
Vivi's father rules.

418
00:23:35,020 --> 00:23:35,850
Yeah,

419
00:23:35,933 --> 00:23:37,317
except there's this guy
named Crocodile who's

420
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:39,257
trying to take over the country right now.

421
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:42,397
And Crocodile's one of the
seven warlords of the sea.

422
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:43,598
Who are those guys?

423
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:47,197
They're pirates who are given
authority by the world government.

424
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:49,497
The government actually supports pirates?

425
00:23:49,580 --> 00:23:50,857
Yeah, pretty weird, huh?

426
00:23:50,940 --> 00:23:53,705
And the seven warlords
are incredibly powerful.

427
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:57,440
You see, they go around defeating
other pirates one by one.

428
00:23:57,760 --> 00:24:00,697
And that's why the government
supports the warlords.

429
00:24:00,780 --> 00:24:04,604
The idea is to have the pirates
get rid of all the other pirates.

430
00:24:06,360 --> 00:24:09,237
I'm really looking forward to
meeting this Crocodile guy.

431
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:11,517
Crocodile is considered a hero back home.

432
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:14,437
He helps get rid of the
pirates who attack Alabasta.

433
00:24:14,520 --> 00:24:17,037
However, his good deeds only
appear good on the surface.

434
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:19,340
He is an evil man. In truth,

435
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:21,737
he's manipulating the
citizens of Alabasta to bring

436
00:24:21,820 --> 00:24:24,637
about his civil war so he
can take over the country.

437
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:27,485
No one has realized what
Crocodile's doing yet.

438
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:28,880
Not the people.

439
00:24:29,140 --> 00:24:31,140
Not even my father. Right.

440
00:24:31,380 --> 00:24:32,397
Well, this should be fun.

441
00:24:32,480 --> 00:24:34,977
All we have to do is beat
up that crocodile guy.

442
00:24:35,060 --> 00:24:38,477
Yes, but in order to do that, we have
to avert the Civil War in Alabasta?

443
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:40,677
and get Baroque works out of the picture.

444
00:24:40,760 --> 00:24:41,590
Baroque works?

445
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:42,920
Oh, yeah.

446
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:45,157
You don't know anything
about them, either.

447
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:47,857
To be honest, I don't understand
what's going on with them myself.

448
00:24:47,940 --> 00:24:51,257
They have a really complicated system
of agents, bosses, and partners.

449
00:24:51,340 --> 00:24:53,516
The system is actually pretty simple.

450
00:24:53,960 --> 00:24:57,195
First, at the very top of
the organization is the boss,

451
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:58,830
Crocodile.

452
00:24:58,980 --> 00:24:59,937
He's known as Mr.

453
00:25:00,020 --> 00:25:00,850
Zero.

454
00:25:00,933 --> 00:25:02,517
There are a total of
12 agents in one animal

455
00:25:02,600 --> 00:25:04,797
who receive orders from the boss directly.

456
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:08,704
For the most part, these 12 male
agents operate as part of a pair

457
00:25:10,740 --> 00:25:12,280
with a female agent. Mr.

458
00:25:12,380 --> 00:25:14,017
One is paired with Miss Doublefinger.

459
00:25:14,100 --> 00:25:14,930
Mr.

460
00:25:15,013 --> 00:25:16,348
Two doesn't actually have a

461
00:25:16,740 --> 00:25:17,880
female partner. Mr.

462
00:25:18,020 --> 00:25:21,177
Three is the candle man we ran
into in Little Garden, right?

463
00:25:21,260 --> 00:25:24,397
That's right, And his partner is
the painter, Miss Golden Week.

464
00:25:24,480 --> 00:25:25,310
Oh, yeah.

465
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:26,600
That little girl.

466
00:25:27,280 --> 00:25:28,110
Mr.

467
00:25:28,193 --> 00:25:29,023
Four is next in line.

468
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:30,877
He's paired up with Miss Merry Christmas.

469
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:33,337
I don't know much more than
that about those two, though.

470
00:25:33,420 --> 00:25:36,280
Then there's that snot
guy. Mr. Five. Snot?

471
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:38,437
Yeah, his snot is explosive. Mr.

472
00:25:38,520 --> 00:25:40,837
Five's entire body can
be used as a weapon.

473
00:25:40,920 --> 00:25:44,217
His partner, Miss Valentine,
has the kilo-kilo fruit powers.

474
00:25:44,300 --> 00:25:47,197
That's the woman who can change
her weight whenever she wants.

475
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:49,097
The agents with code names from Mr.

476
00:25:49,180 --> 00:25:50,010
One through Mr.

477
00:25:50,093 --> 00:25:51,917
Five are known as officer agents.

478
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:54,117
They each possess one of
the Devil Fruit powers,

479
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:57,376
and they are only sent on
the most important missions.

480
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:58,630
Agents Mr.

481
00:25:58,713 --> 00:25:59,543
Six through Mr.

482
00:25:59,626 --> 00:26:01,317
Thirteen have the job of fundraising.

483
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:03,217
They make money for the
organization by heading

484
00:26:03,300 --> 00:26:05,977
up the employees at the
entrance to the Grand Line.

485
00:26:06,060 --> 00:26:09,577
Hey, what about that weird monkey
and chicken pair I ran into?

486
00:26:09,660 --> 00:26:10,490
That's Mr.

487
00:26:10,573 --> 00:26:11,911
Thirteen and Miss Friday.

488
00:26:12,400 --> 00:26:14,597
They're the agency's punishment squad.

489
00:26:14,680 --> 00:26:17,637
They punish any agent who
fails to complete a mission.

490
00:26:17,720 --> 00:26:18,597
And there are more.

491
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:21,597
Under the Officer Agents
are 200 men called Billions,

492
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:23,677
and there are another 1,800 men under the

493
00:26:23,760 --> 00:26:26,289
Frontier Agents that
are known as Millions.

494
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:30,097
Together they make up the secret
crime syndicate Baroque Works.

495
00:26:30,180 --> 00:26:33,597
Let's see, 200 plus
1,800 equals, um, uh...

496
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:35,940
There are 2,000 of them? 2,000!

497
00:26:36,260 --> 00:26:38,142
All right, I think I understand.

498
00:26:38,240 --> 00:26:41,777
When are we going to get to
Alabasta so I can beat up Crocodile?

499
00:26:41,860 --> 00:26:43,977
Uh, I don't think you
get it at all, Loopy.

500
00:26:44,060 --> 00:26:46,697
If Baroque Works' sole objective
is to take over Alabasta.

501
00:26:46,780 --> 00:26:49,797
Alabasta then I can guess what
that must mean the rest of the

502
00:26:49,880 --> 00:26:53,257
officer agents as Phoebe called
them and their subordinates are.

503
00:26:53,340 --> 00:26:56,220
Probably on their way
to Alabasta as we speak.

504
00:26:57,300 --> 00:26:58,130
Yeah

505
00:26:58,860 --> 00:27:03,160
I see so in that case we just
go beat up that's enough Luffy.

506
00:27:03,480 --> 00:27:04,362
Just let it go.

507
00:27:04,460 --> 00:27:05,290
Okay

508
00:27:11,780 --> 00:27:14,480
I'm sorry, Mr. Toot. Mr. Bonclay, sir.

509
00:27:15,460 --> 00:27:17,457
Would you idiots quit playing around?

510
00:27:17,540 --> 00:27:18,370
Damn it!

511
00:27:18,453 --> 00:27:19,317
Are you completely clueless?

512
00:27:19,400 --> 00:27:20,929
Do you even know who I am?

513
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:24,700
I am Bonclay, a Baroque
works officer agent.

514
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:27,677
I strike fear into the
heart of anyone who sees me.

515
00:27:27,760 --> 00:27:30,637
Hey, you, navigator, tell
me something. Yes, sir.

516
00:27:30,720 --> 00:27:35,277
Does that little pea-brain of yours
remember what the boss's exact orders were?

517
00:27:35,360 --> 00:27:36,240
Yes, Mr. Two.

518
00:27:36,380 --> 00:27:37,517
The orders were to kill Mr.

519
00:27:37,600 --> 00:27:41,057
Three on his way along the direct route
between Little Garden and Alabasta.

520
00:27:41,140 --> 00:27:41,970
Okay, then.

521
00:27:42,180 --> 00:27:44,945
Maybe you're not entirely
useless, now are you?

522
00:27:46,060 --> 00:27:49,117
Taking a direct route means that
you travel in a straight line,

523
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:50,217
doesn't it, Navigator?

524
00:27:50,300 --> 00:27:54,197
That's why we went straight from Alabasta
to Little Garden, isn't that right?

525
00:27:54,280 --> 00:27:57,797
But then something seems to have gone wrong
with the plan, now hasn't it, Navigator?

526
00:27:57,880 --> 00:28:00,357
We reach Little Guard
without so much as seeing Mr.

527
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:02,087
Three while on our way here.

528
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:06,660
Not me, that seems to indicate
that you fools missed Mr.

529
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:08,134
Three's ship entirely.

530
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:09,887
No, sir, that can't be true.

531
00:28:10,080 --> 00:28:13,257
Hmm, it sort of sounds like you're
questioning my intelligence.

532
00:28:13,340 --> 00:28:14,340
Not at all, sir.

533
00:28:14,480 --> 00:28:15,420
Be quiet, you.

534
00:28:15,820 --> 00:28:18,760
All we have to do is kill
the pathetic Mr. Three.

535
00:28:19,060 --> 00:28:23,117
It should be an easy mission and one
at which we have no excuse to fail.

536
00:28:23,200 --> 00:28:24,977
We must complete the mission soon.

537
00:28:25,060 --> 00:28:26,420
If we don't, then Mr.

538
00:28:26,520 --> 00:28:30,285
One and his partner will be sent
out to make sure I end up dead.

539
00:28:30,480 --> 00:28:32,040
Clear enough for you!

540
00:28:32,520 --> 00:28:35,997
Now, if you don't want to answer to
me, then you'd better get to work.

541
00:28:36,080 --> 00:28:37,940
Looking for that Mr. Three.

542
00:28:38,960 --> 00:28:42,720
I want this ship going as
fast as it can, you imbeciles!

543
00:28:42,900 --> 00:28:45,194
We're heading to Alabasta immediately!

544
00:28:45,900 --> 00:28:48,360
Yes, sir, Mr. Two, Mr. Monclay, sir!

545
00:28:50,320 --> 00:28:51,150
What's this?

546
00:28:51,520 --> 00:28:54,285
Pirates are attacking
towns inside the kingdom?

547
00:28:55,060 --> 00:28:58,017
Don't they know this country
is protected by crocodile?

548
00:28:58,100 --> 00:29:00,159
Who can tell what they're thinking?

549
00:29:00,560 --> 00:29:05,148
A country where riots are constantly
brewing may be considered an easy target.

550
00:29:07,780 --> 00:29:08,610
You'll go.

551
00:29:10,300 --> 00:29:11,130
Naturally.

552
00:29:11,220 --> 00:29:13,600
I do have a public duty to uphold.

553
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:16,140
How very kind of you, sir.

554
00:29:18,820 --> 00:29:20,420
Yes, I'm a kind man.

555
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:24,017
We warlords are charged with protecting
the public from pirate threats.

556
00:29:24,100 --> 00:29:26,760
We are heroes to these people after all.

557
00:29:54,100 --> 00:29:56,980
As you are with me.

558
00:29:57,760 --> 00:30:02,280
I've grown stronger having you by my side.

559
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:07,400
We've started on an everlasting ride.

560
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:12,500
I'm invincible when your love is near.

561
00:30:13,120 --> 00:30:17,557
When I'm with you I have no fear.

562
00:30:17,640 --> 00:30:24,017
Let's see how far we can make this go.

563
00:30:24,100 --> 00:30:27,297
The world is ours.

564
00:30:27,380 --> 00:30:29,297
Future's pride I know.

565
00:30:29,380 --> 00:30:32,097
I see it shine.

566
00:30:32,180 --> 00:30:33,817
In the distance.

567
00:30:33,900 --> 00:30:35,757
Glistening like water.

568
00:30:35,840 --> 00:30:39,900
When the sun rises in the dawn?
